# The acid's answer (the fourth acid page, ARP x4): its kind (K1), how often (K2), which way (K3), whether it counts bars or loops (K4). The line asks, then answers.
seed 0
wait 500
tap GLO
tap ARP
tap ARP
tap ARP
tap ARP
expect view 11
expect par76 0
# an octave, up one (kind 1 * 5 + direction 3)
spin K1 1
wait 100
expect par151 8
shot answer_page.png
# up two
spin K3 1
wait 100
expect par151 9
# Mirror (kind 4), the direction kept (4): the contour round the line's middle, two octaves up from there
spin K1 3
wait 100
expect par151 24
shot answer_mirror.png
# Reverse, Rotate, Sparse, Accents follow
spin K1 1
wait 100
expect par151 29
shot answer_reverse.png
spin K1 3
wait 100
expect par151 44
# every 4th bar, then before a drum change; the chance
spin K2 2
wait 100
expect par21 2
spin K2 5
wait 100
expect par21 7
spin K4 1
wait 100
expect par76 1
wait 9000
